  "headline": "Magnitude 7.2 Earthquake Strikes Maluku Barat Daya, Indonesia",
  "seoTitle": "Magnitude 7.2 Earthquake Strikes Maluku Barat Daya",
  "metaDescription": "A magnitude 7.2 earthquake has impacted the Maluku Barat Daya region in Indonesia. The national meteorology agency confirms there is no tsunami threat.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "A magnitude 7.2 earthquake was recorded in the Maluku Barat Daya region.",
    "The Indonesian Agency for Meteorology, Climatology, and Geophysics confirmed no tsunami risk.",
    "Initial reports identified the seismic activity as originating from the Benioff zone."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "On November 21, 2026, a significant earthquake measuring magnitude 7.2 struck the Maluku Barat Daya region of Indonesia. Following the event, the national meteorology agency, BMKG, issued an official statement confirming that the seismic activity posed no tsunami threat to the surrounding areas. Technical analysis of the tremor indicated that the event originated from the Benioff zone, a region of subduction where tectonic plates interact. The seismic event was reported by multiple news outlets shortly after it occurred, marking a period of notable geological activity in the Indonesian archipelago. While other minor tremors were reported in separate locations across Indonesia during the same weekend, including in Sulawesi Utara and Papua, the Maluku Barat Daya earthquake remained a primary focal point for disaster monitoring authorities due to its significant magnitude.",
